<!--
  T10 Units Breadth

  HOW MUCH OF D-SI A CLEAN DESIGN CAN USE: a prefix with a negative exponent,
  an affine scale, an explicit dimensionless value, and a US spelling that folds
  to the canonical identifier before it is parsed.

  A UNIT TEST DESIGN. Bundled with the app and read-only: suite [25]
  asserts what this file is supposed to prove, so editing it here
  changes what the harness tests.
-->
<gorp name="T10 Units Breadth">
  <!-- nos-uml-state {"mode":"ai-design","title":"T10 Units Breadth","layout":{"ut.units.Probe":{"x":60,"y":60,"w":320,"h":200},"ut.units.Read":{"x":460,"y":60,"w":280,"h":140},"ut.units.Reading":{"x":820,"y":60,"w":280,"h":140}}} -->

  <comment view="class">How much of D-SI a clean design can use, on one model: a prefixed unit with a negative exponent (\kilo\metre\hour\tothe{-1}, shown as km/h), an affine scale (\degreecelsius), an explicit dimensionless value (\one), and a US spelling in the SI namespace (meter) that folds to the canonical identifier before it is parsed.

All four grade, and all four are legal on a real that collapses Monotone.</comment>
  <expect>Check finds nothing on any of the four rows and Run comes back OK.

Each chip must read as maths — km/h, °C — while the file keeps the canonical D-SI spelling; hover shows that spelling and the grade.</expect>
  <model namespace="ut.units.Probe">
    <variables>
      <variable name="speed" type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\kilo\metre\hour\tothe{-1}" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="temp"  type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\degreecelsius" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="ratio" type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="height" type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="meter" namespace="SI"/></variable>
    </variables>
  </model>

  <algorithm namespace="ut.units.Read">
    <input  model="ut.units.Probe" />
    <output model="ut.units.Reading" />
    <operations>
      <operation name="read" returns="double" />
    </operations>
  </algorithm>

  <model namespace="ut.units.Reading">
    <variables>
      <variable name="value" type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
    </variables>
  </model>
</gorp>
